#: ../../layers/recurrents/bi_lstm.rst:3
msgid "Bi-Directional LSTM (Bi-LSTM)"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.recurrent.bi_lstm.BiLSTM:1 of
msgid "Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory (BiLSTM) layer for sequence modeling."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.recurrent.bi_lstm.BiLSTM:3 of
msgid ""
"The BiLSTM layer processes a whole sequence in both the forward and the "
"reverse time direction and concatenates the hidden states of both "
"directions per step. This allows the network to capture information from "
"both past and future context, resulting in richer representations. About "
"LSTM, please see :class:`marquetry.layers.LSTM`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../layers/recurrents/bi_lstm.rst
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.recurrent.bi_lstm.BiLSTM:9 of
msgid "The size of the hidden state in each LSTM layer."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.recurrent.bi_lstm.BiLSTM:11 of
msgid "The size of the input data."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.recurrent.bi_lstm.BiLSTM:16 of
msgid "in_size:"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.recurrent.bi_lstm.BiLSTM:17 of
msgid ""
"This is automatically determined from the input data shape and does not "
"need to be specified except a special use case."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.recurrent.bi_lstm.BiLSTM:20 of
msgid ""
"Unlike the step-wise :class:`marquetry.layers.LSTM`, this layer takes the"
" **whole sequence at once** as a 3-dim array ``(batch, time, features)`` "
"because the reverse direction needs the future steps. The internal states"
" are reset at the beginning of every call, so each call processes its "
"sequence independently."
msgstr ""

